<worksheet xml:id="ws-9">
    <title>The T-N-B Frame</title>
    <exercise workspace="6.0in">
      <p>
        For the vector-valued function
        <md>
            \mathbf{r}(t) = \langle 2\sin(t), 5t, 2\cos(t)\rangle
        </md>
        find the unit vectors <m>\mathbf{T}(t)</m>, <m>\mathbf{N}(t)</m> and <m>\mathbf{B}(t)</m>. Then find the curvature function. Evaluate all of them at the point <m>(\pi/4,3,\pi/4)</m>.
    </p> 
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="3.0in">
        <p>
            Describe, using your own words, what the vectors <m>\mathbf{T}(t)</m>, <m>\mathbf{N}(t)</m> and <m>\mathbf{B}(t)</m> tell you about the curve. (A picture may be helpful in your description.)
        </p>
    </exercise>
    
</worksheet>